        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background-color:#101a36;background-image:linear-gradient(color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 26%,transparent) 0.12cqw,transparent 0.12cqw),linear-gradient(90deg,color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 26%,transparent) 0.12cqw,transparent 0.12cqw),linear-gradient(color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 12%,transparent) 0.08cqw,transparent 0.08cqw),linear-gradient(90deg,color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 12%,transparent) 0.08cqw,transparent 0.08cqw);background-size:10cqw 10cqw,10cqw 10cqw,2cqw 2cqw,2cqw 2cqw;font-family:Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;color:#ffffff'><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;top:3.4cqw;font:800 1.5cqw/1.2 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#75ffe4'>TWILITE / AI STARTER</div><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;right:4cqw;top:6.2cqw;font:850 6.2cqw/1.02 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>Start with your AI</div><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;right:4cqw;top:14.34cqw;font:400 2.5cqw/1.3 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#f7faff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>Talk with your AI about what you want to make. It will put it here.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;top:19.4cqw;font:400 1.7cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#75ffe4'>Six steps. Your AI does the typing.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;right:4cqw;top:23cqw;bottom:23.2cqw;box-sizing:border-box;border-radius:0.5cqw;background:color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 7%,#101a36);border:.3cqw solid color-mix(in srgb,#75ffe4 28%,#101a36)'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:4cqw;right:4cqw;bottom:2.4cqw;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.8cqw 2.4cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.3 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#75ffe4'><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>1</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Start your AI.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Click the Twilite icon in the top bar. It copies what your AI needs to know. Paste it into a chat with your AI. It will tell you it understands, and ask what you want to make.</span></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>2</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Talk it through.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Tell your AI about a project, a story, a plan, or an idea. Talk until there is something worth keeping. It may offer to put it in a graph, or you can ask for one.</span></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>3</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Bring its reply back.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Click the paste icon in the toolbar, paste what your AI wrote, and choose Run. Then ask for more in the same chat and paste each reply the same way, or change a card yourself.</span></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>4</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Look around.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Zoom out until each card shows only its title, then in until it shows everything. One graph, three sizes. Click a card to select it.</span></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>5</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Save it.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Saving is part of the editor. With it, click the save icon in the top bar, then Save As: Save locally downloads the file, Save to GitHub keeps it in your repository. <a href='tlz://twilite.zone/tutorial/how-to-guides/github-from-nothing/root.node' style='color:#75ffe4'>New to GitHub? Set it up from nothing.</a></span></span></div><div style='display:flex;gap:1cqw;align-items:baseline'><span style='color:#75ffe4;font:800 1.6cqw/1.1 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif'>6</span><span><b style='color:#ffffff'>Come back.</b> <span style='font-weight:400;color:#f7faff'>Another day, choose Open graph from the same menu. Your graph is as you left it.</span></span></div><div style='grid-column:1 / -1;margin-top:.6cqw;font:400 1.2cqw/1.3 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#75ffe4'>It worked when the stage fills with what you described.</div></div><div style='position:absolute;right:4cqw;top:3cqw;display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;font:700 1.9cqw/1.2 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;white-space:nowrap'><a href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/documentation/what-is-a-graph/root.node' style='color:#75ffe4;text-decoration:none'>What a graph is →</a><a href='tlz://twilite.zone/root.node' style='color:#75ffe4;text-decoration:none'>The Twilite Zone →</a></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The environment: the room the graph's work sits in. This poster teaches; delete it and the graph stands on plain graph paper."
      }
    }
